\label{defn:locally-retractile}
    A space $X$ with an action of a topological group $G$ is \emph{$G$-locally retractile} 
    if for each $x \in X$ there is a neighbourhood $U \subset X$ and a map $\xi\colon U \to G$ such that $\xi(u).x = u$ holds for all $u \in U$.

