\label{prop:ess-red-contratible}
    Suppose~$\scl{M}$ is not irreducible. 
    Then the classifying space of the poset of non-empty cut systems is contractible, i.e.~$\|\mathrm{Cut}^{\neq \emptyset}_\bullet(M)\| \simeq *$.

A cut system $\Sigma$ on a $3$-manifold $M$ is called \emph{separating}
if each component of $\scl{M \smash{\mid} \Sigma}$ is irreducible. Let $\mathrm{Sep}(M) \subseteq \mathrm{Cut}(M)$ denote the subspace of separating cut systems.

For $q \ge 1$ we say that a cut system $\Sigma$ is \emph{$q$-separating}
if each component of $\scl{M \smash{\mid} \Sigma}$ has at most $q$ prime factors. 
Let $\qsep{q}(M) \subseteq \mathrm{Cut}(M)$ denote the subspace of $q$-separating cut systems.

Then $\mathrm{Sep}(M)$ and $\qsep{q}(M)$ are posets with respect to $\subseteq$ and we denote their nerves by $\mathrm{Sep}_\bullet(M) \subset \mathrm{Cut}_\bullet(M)$ and $\qsep{q}_\bullet(M) \subset \mathrm{Cut}_\bullet(M)$.

\label{lem:reversing-coorientation}
